Next we’ll create templates/configmap.yaml.

Helm Step 1 — ConfigMap Template

Create:

D:\GitHub\FastApiArgoProject\helm\medical-api\templates\configmap.yaml

add:

apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: {{ include "medical-api.fullname" . }}-config
  labels:
    {{- include "medical-api.labels" . | nindent 4 }}
data:
  APP_NAME: {{ .Values.config.appName | quote }}
  APP_VERSION: {{ .Values.config.appVersion | quote }}
  ENVIRONMENT: {{ .Values.config.environment | quote }}



The template reads values from values.yaml:

.Values.config.appName
        ↓
config:
  appName: "Medical Appointment API"

  mportant Helm syntax:

{{ ... }} — evaluate a Helm expression.
.Values — values loaded from values.yaml.
quote — surround the result with quotes.
include — call a reusable helper from _helpers.tpl.
nindent 4 — insert a newline and indent by four spaces.

We don’t hardcode namespace: medical-dev. Helm will use the namespace supplied during installation.

